  "description": "WOYFOH crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H76 Cl2 Ho4 Mn2 N6 O22,8(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 7 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.539-3.950 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.82-111.91°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [{LMn(Cl)(μ3-OH)Ho2(μ3-OH)(μ-Piv)2}2]·8MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
